/* ===========================================================================
   app.rc - resource script
   ===========================================================================

   This file embeds the manifest into the .exe.

   The two numbers matter:

     1   = CREATEPROCESS_MANIFEST_RESOURCE_ID.
           For an .exe the manifest MUST have resource ID 1. ID 2 is the one
           used for DLLs, and Windows will simply ignore a manifest with the
           wrong ID - you get no error, just the unthemed Windows-95 look and
           a lot of confusion.

     24  = RT_MANIFEST, the resource TYPE for manifests.

   Build with:
       windres -O coff -i res/app.rc -o build/app.res.o

   Then link build/app.res.o like any other object file.

   NOTE: keep this file plain ASCII with no byte-order mark. The windres
   preprocessor chokes on a UTF-8 BOM with a confusing syntax error.
   =========================================================================== */

1 24 "app.manifest"
